{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CSUfuCh8A4HYGkDe1spP6m","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I now have comprehensive information about the project. Let me compile the findings:\n\n## Project Structure & Key Configurations — solver-trace-ablation\n\n### 1. EXPERIMENT PLAN\n**File:** `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_3/projects/solver-trace-ablation/experiment_plan.yaml`\n\nThe experiment plan has 12 planned experiments across three priority levels:\n\n**P0 (Must-run, ~13h GPU):**\n- `plan_001`: FOL single-logic GRPO, execution-only reward (500 steps, K=8, 3 seeds) — baseline\n- `plan_002`: FOL single-logic GRPO, execution+STA reward (500 steps, K=8, 3 seeds) — primary validation\n- `plan_003`: FOL held-out evaluation comparing plan_001 vs plan_002 checkspoints\n- `plan_004`: STA O(1) vs O(N) ablation (500 steps, 1 seed) — negative result documentation\n- `plan_005`: STA reward weight ablation: test α/β ratios (0.3/0.7, 0.5/0.5, 0.7/0.3) + sigmoid curriculum vs fixed\n\n**P1 (Important, ~8h GPU):**\n- `plan_006-008`: Prolog single-logic and multi-logic GRPO experiments\n- `plan_009`: SFT baseline for comparison\n- `plan_012`: Hacking characterization (manual annotation of 200 outputs per condition)\n\n**P2 (Nice-to-have, ~9h GPU):**\n- `plan_010`: SMT-LIB single-logic\n- `plan_011`: Qwen3-8B scaling (1 seed)\n\n### 2. REGISTRY (COMPLETED EXPERIMENTS & METRICS)\n**File:** `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_3/projects/solver-trace-ablation/registry.yaml`\n\n**Completed experiments (as of 2026-05-13):**\n\n**Phase 0 Baselines:**\n- `sta-phase0-baseline` (✓ success): Base Qwen3-4B on 100 FOLIO FOL problems\n  - Metrics: prove_rate=0.12, mean_isr=0.0641, isr_std=0.1983, isr_range=[0, 0.889]\n  - Effective prove_rate (excluding XOR)=0.182, avg_time=3.4s per sample\n\n- `sta-gt-isr-baseline` (✓ success): Ground-truth ISR on same 100 samples\n  - Metrics: gt_prove_rate=0.18, gt_mean_isr=0.5588, gt_median=0.6125, range=[0.14, 1.00]\n  - Represents 8.7x gap: model ISR 0.064 vs GT ISR 0.559\n\n**Phase 1 (100-step GRPO pilots):**\n- `sta-phase1-exec-only-r5` (✓ success): 100 steps, K=8, seed=42\n  - Metrics: prove_rate=0.15125, mean_isr=0.1475, last_20_prove_rate=0.2, last_20_isr_mean=0.2\n  - Reward: isr_pr_ratio_last20=1.0 (ISR equals prove_rate — binary signal)\n  - Checkpoint: `/root/autodl-tmp/outputs/grpo_exec_only/`\n\n- `sta-phase1-exec-sta-r5` (✓ success): 100 steps, K=8, seed=42, full continuous STA\n  - Metrics: prove_rate=0.1 (lower!), mean_isr=0.04347, last_20_prove_rate=0.15, last_20_isr_mean=0.04956\n  - Reward: isr_pr_ratio_overall=0.43, isr_pr_ratio_last20=0.33 (significant decoupling!)\n  - Step time: ~10.13s (7% overhead vs exec-only's 9.44s)\n  - **Key finding**: ISR/PR ratio fell from 64% to 33%, indicating reward hacking detection\n\n### 3. GRPO TRAINING CONFIGURATIONS\n**Files:** `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_3/projects/solver-trace-ablation/artifacts/grpo_exec_only.yaml` and `grpo_exec_sta.yaml`\n\n**Common hyperparameters (both configs):**\n```yaml\nnum_steps: 100\nper_device_batch_size: 4\ngradient_accumulation_steps: 2\nnum_generations: 4              # K parameter for within-group sampling\nmax_completion_length: 512\nlearning_rate: 1.0e-6\nseed: 42\nsolver: prover9\ndata_path: data/proofwriter_fol_500.jsonl\n```\n\n**Execution-only configuration:**\n```yaml\nexec_weight: 1.0\nsta_weight: 0.0\nreward_mode: execution_only\n```\n\n**Execution+STA configuration:**\n```yaml\nexec_weight: 0.5                 # α (execution weight)\nsta_weight: 0.5                  # β (STA weight) — equal weighting in Phase 1\nreward_mode: execution_sta\n```\n\n**Key notes from decisions.yaml:**\n- Phase 1 r4 tested `sta_weight: 0.0` with `fast_isr_fol` (O(1) tautology check) — **failed, no signal**\n- Phase 1 r5 switched to full continuous STA with `sta_weight: 0.5` — **succeeded**\n- Planned Phase 1.x: test lower weights (sta_weight=0.1) and bonus mode `r = exec × (1 + α × ISR)` to address prove_rate regression\n\n### 4. STA REWARD IMPLEMENTATION DETAILS\n**File:** `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_3/projects/solver-trace-ablation/artifacts/train_grpo.py` (lines 105-184)\n\n**Reward function:**\n```python\ndef make_reward_fn(reward_mode, solver, exec_weight=0.5, sta_weight=0.5):\n    # For \"execution_only\":\n    result = fast_sta_reward({}, cleaned, solver, \n                            execution_weight=1.0, sta_weight=0.0, timeout=5)\n    reward_val = result[\"execution_reward\"]\n    \n    # For \"execution_sta\":\n    result = fast_sta_reward({}, cleaned, solver,\n                            execution_weight=exec_weight, sta_weight=sta_weight, timeout=5)\n    reward_val = result[\"combined_reward\"]\n```\n\n**ISR computation:**\n- ISR is extracted as `result.get(\"sta_reward\", 0.0)` — continuous value in [0, 1]\n- Baseline ISR: 0.064 (base model), 0.559 (ground-truth)\n- Phase 1 r5: ISR mean = 0.1475 (exec-only), 0.04347 (exec-sta)\n- ISR range observed: [0.125, 0.889] on proved samples\n\n**Metrics tracked per step:**\n```\nparse_rate = parsed / total\nprove_rate = proved / total\nmean_isr = isr_sum / total\n```\n\n### 5. REGISTRY METRICS (CONSOLIDATED)\n\n| Experiment | prove_rate | mean_isr | last_20_prove | last_20_isr | isr/pr_ratio | notes |\n|------------|-----------|----------|---------------|------------|-------------|--------|\n| baseline (phase0) | 0.12 | 0.0641 | — | — | — | 100 samples |\n| GT baseline | 0.18 | 0.5588 | — | — | — | upper bound |\n| exec-only r5 | 0.1513 | 0.1475 | 0.20 | 0.20 | 1.00 | isr ≡ pr |\n| exec-sta r5 | 0.10 | 0.0435 | 0.15 | 0.0496 | 0.33 | hacking detected |\n\n### 6. CURRICULUM & WEIGHT SCHEDULE (PLANNED)\n**References in documentation:**\n\nFrom `docs/IDEA_BRIEF.md`:\n- **Planned sigmoid curriculum**: \"structural reward weight follows sigmoid interpolation from 0→λ_max, allowing execution reward to dominate early before 